(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gates/src/docLedger.asl#" :text "Loads, merges and looks up D150 doc ledger rows (:doc :symbol \"path#name\" :text \"...\"), reusing docExtract's ledger routing so a lookup always reads the file an extraction would have written to. Malformed rows are typed errors, not skipped. A symbol with an empty name after '#' is a module doc; a dotted name Type.field is a field doc; a bare Lline name is a free comment with no owning definition and always resolves.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gates/src/docLedger.asl#DocRow.symbol" :text "path#name, path# for a module doc, path#Type.field for a field doc, path#Lline for a comment with no owning definition")
