(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gates/src/gates.asl#collectDirectoryFiles" :text "find exits non-zero when a root is missing or a subdirectory is unreadable, and its partial listing then hides files; that exit is an error naming the directory and find's stderr, never an empty or partial list")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gates/src/gates.asl#allowlistedPaths" :text "foreign means audit.py's langFromHead: binary magic, then #! interpreter, then a recognized foreign-language extension; .sample, .txt, .json, .gz etc are data fixtures, not foreign code, and are never flagged; an exact tracked path that is genuinely foreign (a vendored .c probe, an allowlisted .sh gate) is exempt only when scripts/audit/foreignAllowlist.asn names it, so the allowlist on disk stays the one source of truth instead of a hard-coded path; a missing, unparseable, malformed or entry-less allowlist, an unlistable directory, or an unreadable candidate file, is a gate failure, not a silent pass")
